  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pulse Lab Jakarta Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pulse Lab Jakarta (PLJ) was data innovation initiative in the Asia&#x2013;Pacific region. The Lab developed data driven and AI enabled prototypes to support sustainable development and humanitarian action, drawing on big data analytics and human centred design. PLJ was established as a partnership between the United Nations, through UN Global Pulse, and the Government of Indonesia, through the Ministry of National Development Planning (BAPPENAS).

PLJ contributed to several Government of Indonesia priorities, including strengthening the Ministry of Health&#x2019;s analytical capacity during the COVID 19 response; supporting national efforts to build a more inclusive digital economy, particularly for vulnerable and underserved groups; and assisting Bappenas to establish a low carbon advanced analytics function to help ministries to analyse climate forecasts and develop long term, evidence based climate policies.</narrative>
  </description>
