  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia through a joint data innovation facility of the UN and Indonesia&#x2019;s government developed a dynamic data dashboard to map Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises&#x2019; (MSME) challenges and geospatial distribution, facilitating informed policymaking. This dashboard boosted social protection by enabling accurate identification of COVID-19 cash transfer beneficiaries and integrating MSME support programs. Operational enhancements can be seen in the government adoption of the dashboard and the recruitment of their first data scientist, resulting in a fortified data management system. A service blueprint was created to illustrate the complete process including the recommendations to improve the dashboard for future use.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia through a joint facility of the UN and Indonesia&#x2019;s government supported the Ministry of Health to analyse data to trace the pandemic&#x2019;s spread, monitor population health, predict disease severity and resulting demand, and provide optimized medical solutions to the public. The support assisted health care managers in presenting a solution for optimizing resources to meet fast-changing demand, such as volume of patients, critical care availability, number of beds, ventilator availability. The facility also combined health data analytics with Artificial Intelligence (AI) to effectively capture information on vulnerable groups like people with disabilities.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
